# West and south: the Grimtotem horns, the Woodpaw alphas -------------------------------------------

do 2974
tip The Grimtotem camp west of Camp Mojache is the closest. Almost every Grimtotem drops a horn, often two; the raiders cast a net that roots you.
do 2863
tip Each alpha stands in the middle of a small gnoll camp with two or three guards. More camps lie around 71-74,56, south of the little lake near the battle map, and alphas respawn quickly.
turnin 2863
accept 2902
turnin 2974
accept 2976
tip Keep the Crate of Grimtotem Horns for Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar.

# South-east: the old key, the battle plans -----------------------------------------------------------

accept 95599 at 76.6,48.0 icon pickup "Take the Old Key from the Old Crate south-east of Camp Mojache"
tip The Old Crate stands next to the tent.
turnin 95599
tip The Old Chest lies under water at 79.2,49.4. Handing in the key makes three elementals appear and attack: be ready.
turnin 2902
tip The battle plans lie on a crate at the camp with a bonfire (the others have campfires), around 71,55. Pull the five or six gnolls around it one or two at a time: opening the plans takes a few seconds and any hit stops it.
accept 2903
turnin 2903
accept 7730
accept 7731

# The Zukk'ash hive, the southern Gordunni, Feral Scar Vale and the coast ----------------------------

do 7730 bg
do 7731
tip Stinglasher (level 47) patrols between the two entrances of the Zukk'ash hive, inside and out, wrapped in a poison cloud: he hits harder than the other wasps. Keep a cooldown for him.
do 7730
do 2979 bg
do 2980.1
tip Follow the road south-west over the bridge: the Gordunni hold the ruins on the left (Ruins of Isildien).
tip Shamans are few and spawn slowly: kill every one you see. Clearing the mobs around the little stone gazebo (a level 46 Warlord stands in it) brings more shamans there.
do 2980.2
do 2741 at 57.1,76.3 icon pickup "Take a Hippogryph Egg from the nests (for the Super Egg-O-Matic)"
tip Only if you have The Super Egg-O-Matic from Gadgetzan; otherwise skip it. The nests are up the hill behind the ruins in the far south (around 57-59,75-76), and you can carry only one egg.
do 2979
tip Only Gordunni Mage-Lords drop the orb, rarely (about 3%), and each of you needs one: kill every Mage-Lord you meet in the ruins.
tip If no orb has dropped once the ogre kills are done, skip Dark Ceremony (right-click its step) rather than farm it for hours.
do 2980.3
tip The maulers guard the ogre camp further north, with more warlocks.
do 2822
tip The yetis of Feral Scar Vale (south of the road past Dire Maul, through the cave mouth around 55,56) drop a hide about 40% of the time; skinners get a second hide by skinning them.
accept 2766
tip The OOX-22/FE Distress Beacon is a rare drop of almost any mob in Feralas. Only one of you found it? Share the quest. Neither? Skip the OOX-22/FE steps, here and in Booty Bay.
turnin 2766
tip The robot waits just past the first part of the yeti cave, in a small clearing before the next cave: kill the yetis on the way in, they respawn quickly.
tip Both of you must hand in Find OOX-22/FE! before either of you accepts the escort, or the second one can't join it.
accept 2767
do 2767 at 45.6,43.4 icon text "Escort OOX-22/FE to the dock on the Forgotten Coast"
tip Start the escort only when both of you have the quest. It is hard: three ambushes come along the way. Three yetis (46) just outside the cave before the road, three gorillas (43) after the robot turns north on the main road, then four gnolls (41-43, one a caster) at the fork after the stone bridge by a waterfall. Save your long cooldowns for the gnolls.
tip Let the robot take a hit before you pull everything off it, or it keeps walking and leaves you fighting behind. If it doesn't move at all, another player is escorting it: wait for it to come back.
tip Players on WoW Forever have reported the robot refusing the escort ("You don't meet the requirements"). If that happens, skip the escort and its turn-in in Booty Bay.
do 3520 bg mobs 5308 at 46.9,48.3
tip Kill a Rogue Vale Screecher, use Yeh'kinya's Bramble on its corpse, then talk to the Screecher Spirit that appears (only if you have the quest). One bramble counts for everyone nearby in the party, so the two of you need only three spirits in all. More screechers fly north of the Feathermoon dock, around 45,40.
do 97378
tip Mirrorscale, a level 48 wind serpent, spawns under the bridge just west of Dire Maul (about 49,46), roughly every 3 minutes.
hearth npc 7737

